  "note": "Annual election of one third of the council (three of nine seats), held on Monday 15 January 1900; the paper calls the members town commissioners. Mr M'Knight was returning and presiding officer and the result was given about ten o'clock. Two of the old members were re-elected, and Mr Nugent succeeded in having one of his nominees, J. W. Campbell, elected; Frank English stood as an independent. No party labels are printed."
